<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Free National Movement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1971">1971</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Free National Movement is a political party in the Bahamas, founded in 1971 by opponents of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lynden-pindling">Lynden Pindling</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/progressive-liberal-party">Progressive Liberal Party</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hubert-ingraham">Hubert Ingraham</a> it won the 1992 general election, ending a quarter of a century of PLP government. It has since alternated in power with the PLP, governing again under Ingraham from 2007 to 2012 and under Hubert Minnis from 2017 to 2021.</p></div>
